     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is dangerous.** 1000 mg is five times the 200 mg daily maximum. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've told me you're a financial analyst, not a clinician. Only a licensed prescriber can verify an order that is this far outside the normal range.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- If a physician or other prescriber really intends this dose, they can enter it themselves. Pharmacy will probably review it and may call them to check it.\n- If the dose came from a transcription or typo error, the prescriber can send me the corrected order. For example, 100 mg once daily would be within the normal range. I can enter it once they've confirmed.\n\nI'm glad to help with the order once a prescriber has confirmed it."
      }
     ],
